NOTICE

This skill (mcpe-native-modding) teaches the methodology of the open-source
BedrockTools project (https://github.com/RadiantByte/BedrockTools) for the
preloader runtime, and documents the BreezeAPI runtime
(https://github.com/wisebreeze/BreezeAPI) for Dobby-based hooking with
embedded QuickJS scripting.

The hook/patch/signature/build patterns for the preloader runtime are
derived from BedrockTools' code and documentation. This skill is licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see the repository root LICENSE).

Referenced upstream projects:

- BedrockTools (https://github.com/RadiantByte/BedrockTools) — methodology
  source for the preloader runtime.
- preloader-android (https://github.com/LiteLDev/preloader-android) — the
  preloader SDK.
- LeviLaunchroid (https://github.com/LiteLDev/LeviLaunchroid) — the
  launcher for the preloader runtime.
- BreezeAPI (https://github.com/wisebreeze/BreezeAPI) — the Dobby-based
  runtime with QuickJS.
- Dobby (https://github.com/jmpews/Dobby) — inline hook engine used by
  BreezeAPI.
- QuickJS (https://bellard.org/quickjs/) — JavaScript engine embedded in
  BreezeAPI.

Use responsibly: hook/patch only binaries you are authorized to modify,
keep work to learning/personal use, and respect the game's terms of
service.
